  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened national social protection system in Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ghana has implemented several programmes with social protection prospects. Amongst the social protection programmes/schemes is the availability of health insurance through the National Health Insurance Scheme (NHIS), by eliminating registration fees. However, some farming householders do not know how to apply for the registration fee waiver and, additionally, accessing the NHIS does not necessarily translate into being able to access quality health services due to obstacles such as lack of transport and the availability of health centres with essential infrastructure (e.g. water, electricity). In addition, a lot of households/families with incidents of child labour does not have access to health insurances due to the challenges highlighted above.
The interventions focuses on improving access to social protection (health insurance) and other social services to households affected by or at risk of forced labour and child labour.</narrative>
  </description>
